{:edb/db-before-t 1488 :edb/db-after-t 1489 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534801 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:22:08.767Z" 13194139534801 true] [17592186096421 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)" 13194139534801 true] [17592186096421 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)" 13194139534801 false] [17592186096617 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310834 13194139534801 true] [17592186096617 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310893 13194139534801 true] [17592186096618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310841 13194139534801 true] [17592186096618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310848 13194139534801 true] [17592186096618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310855 13194139534801 true] [17592186096618 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310900 13194139534801 true] [17592186096619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310879 13194139534801 true] [17592186096619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310886 13194139534801 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310862 13194139534801 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310869 13194139534801 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310872 13194139534801 true] [17592186097222 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2(x-1)?$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186097222 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x - 1)$?" 13194139534801 false] [17592186097222 1145 "Integrating $y'=2(x-1)$ gives\n$$y=(x-1)^2+C.$$\nThe solution curves are upward-opening parabolas, all with symmetry axis $x=1$, differing only by vertical translation. Select the diagram showing this family; its vertices all have $x$-coordinate $1$." 13194139534801 false] [17592186097222 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-1)^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/92a2dbaa5726e6a1ab83fa879ad7b630b05e68a8e366db214b74d85269a849a9.png)" 13194139534801 true] [17592186292742 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)" 13194139534801 true] [17592186292742 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)" 13194139534801 false] [17592186292759 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)" 13194139534801 true] [17592186292759 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)" 13194139534801 false] [17592186310834 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310835 13194139534801 true] [17592186310834 1089 "q-119033" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310834 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534801 true] [17592186310834 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+3{e}^{-x}=0.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310834 1113 #uuid "57dad966-30e8-503a-bfa2-6fa76bd6e7c3" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310834 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-{e}^{-x})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310836 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310837 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310838 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310839 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310840 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310838 13194139534801 true] [17592186310835 1110 #uuid "65047499-d7aa-5e87-a285-a163c3ea9768" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310836 1034 "f(x)={e}^{x-3}+C" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310836 1111 #uuid "0e22fabc-f00d-55d9-9962-dafaaf9c9bc3" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310837 1034 "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}+C" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310837 1111 #uuid "f88798d6-517c-5b79-a201-0056dab29f59" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310838 1034 "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310838 1111 #uuid "f6c3095a-d173-5623-b174-54c28052da88" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310839 1034 "f(x)={e}^{-3x}+C" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310839 1111 #uuid "902819ca-98fd-5ff8-8e41-c5b7a45d54be" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310840 1034 "f(x)=-{e}^{-x/3}+C" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310840 1111 #uuid "df15a2d9-9652-570c-861e-dd19e7a11844" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310842 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1089 "q-119038" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1100 "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{-2x}.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1113 #uuid "795b711d-ea65-5cb8-87a2-70f0c9e6f190" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310841 1145 "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int {e}^{-2x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+C \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{-2x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310843 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310844 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310845 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310846 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310847 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310844 13194139534801 true] [17592186310842 1110 #uuid "fc0e6c8d-b9b0-5a01-9ad3-7b6d7b3d5bd8" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310843 1034 "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310843 1111 #uuid "9bfd9fab-eee2-5452-9cef-7e428deaaf4e" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310844 1034 "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310844 1111 #uuid "a5162f30-f9f8-56f0-87e3-c050745c20d2" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310845 1034 "y={e}^{-2x}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310845 1111 #uuid "72905702-3042-5474-a8ed-03080ecbc5a9" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310846 1034 "y=-{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+Dx" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310846 1111 #uuid "1547bd12-2561-5d09-8e55-3a2f8e1e5a46" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310847 1034 "y=2{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310847 1111 #uuid "20516aab-1dff-53db-99bc-d2fc0df33732" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310849 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1089 "q-119039" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1100 "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=20{x}^{3}.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1113 #uuid "9f503fbb-9abb-5178-8aa2-5b5187c150ec" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310848 1145 "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =20\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310850 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310851 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310852 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310853 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310854 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310852 13194139534801 true] [17592186310849 1110 #uuid "91d2e992-27c7-55a0-8f73-5da87db86e86" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310850 1034 "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310850 1111 #uuid "5fa3cfa8-b4c4-558d-a142-c62d743f5b21" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310851 1034 "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310851 1111 #uuid "4ca552f4-ecd4-57e1-9e64-1b1512271b19" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310852 1034 "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310852 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310852 1111 #uuid "d0ed767e-2ea4-5874-ab05-b9cf32e3ae85" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310853 1034 "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310853 1111 #uuid "d6506a3e-7af8-5c03-b770-4638a91d2e5f" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310854 1034 "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310854 1111 #uuid "34f2e060-bb98-5844-aedd-c02a5b5cd771" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310856 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1089 "q-119042" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1100 "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6x=8{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1113 #uuid "70bd483b-e098-5a66-894e-b6127c602eb9" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310855 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{x/2}-6x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{e}^{x/2}-6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(2{e}^{x/2})-6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =16\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =16(2{e}^{x/2})-3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310857 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310858 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310859 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310860 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310861 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310859 13194139534801 true] [17592186310856 1110 #uuid "7949e831-bd6a-52f4-909d-5add3ea77214" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310857 1034 "y=16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310857 1111 #uuid "bfdb6a31-56b7-5da3-833d-537f58cf0991" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310858 1034 "y=32{e}^{x/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310858 1111 #uuid "ca1ed765-8da8-56b2-b6b6-dca7f52887e8" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310859 1034 "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310859 1111 #uuid "13e8808d-c92a-513d-9c5e-12c9e4d8a142" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310860 1034 "y=8{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310860 1111 #uuid "ae10f626-d26f-5227-90c5-6378973d2c40" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310861 1034 "y=16{e}^{x/2}+{x}^{3}+Cx+D" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310861 1111 #uuid "9427e188-e12b-5caf-9d4b-376fba24a6f3" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310863 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1089 "q-119075" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}+{e}^{-2x}=8x$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1.$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1113 #uuid "628de31a-0131-5bc3-8d96-da42a627646b" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310862 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8x-{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8x-{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})+C \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =4(0)^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2(0)}}{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310864 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310865 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310866 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310867 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310868 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310868 13194139534801 true] [17592186310863 1110 #uuid "91e56ac5-ece3-5602-baa2-12a9baa3ced5" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310864 1034 "y=2{x}^{2}-2{e}^{-2x}+3" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310864 1111 #uuid "82ac090d-6697-5663-8182-c7a3855f22e5" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310865 1034 "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310865 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310865 1111 #uuid "ce92a6ae-f1fb-5e9a-81d8-2f58ee08fdc1" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310866 1034 "y=8{x}^{2}+2{e}^{-2x}-1" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310866 1111 #uuid "673c97ea-db18-5cf4-8ac2-16a511a9cff9" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310867 1034 "y=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310867 1111 #uuid "91cc5a24-4a6d-57ad-b0a1-131a6d449488" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310868 1034 "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310868 1111 #uuid "20d08c01-ca11-5f10-886e-0e0b05769ca7" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310870 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1089 "q-352075" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$f(x)=\\,${{field-1}}" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1113 #uuid "70c980cd-81fa-5291-8d3c-a2e45e768133" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310869 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+C \\\\ 2 & =3(1)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1.\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310871 13194139534801 true] [17592186310870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534801 true] [17592186310870 1041 "field-1" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310871 13194139534801 true] [17592186310870 1110 #uuid "4979caa1-2149-50a8-be09-1cac467c30fc" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310871 1034 "3\\cos(x)-1" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310871 1111 #uuid "08fb583b-06b4-5e74-b8c7-7ee87b6ec923" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310873 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1089 "q-50159" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-2.$\n\n$$\n(1+2x){f}^{′}(x)-2=0.\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1113 #uuid "0441f582-d4ce-5255-9837-f92abb18b7b0" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310872 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=(1+2x).$ Then $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2\\cdot 0|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2.\n$$" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310874 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310875 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310876 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310877 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310878 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1041 "selection" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310876 13194139534801 true] [17592186310873 1110 #uuid "de175db1-df03-514c-b7db-688891b19665" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310874 1034 "f(x)=2x-2" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310874 1111 #uuid "2d847047-23bf-53d1-a78a-76fd499a9bab" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310875 1034 "f(x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true] [17592186310875 1111 #uuid "a06ecdcf-6765-50a7-8618-93b2d122a043" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310876 1034 "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" 13194139534801 true] [17592186310876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534801 true